
title:: SMuFLtools
summary:: a convenience class for searching SMuFL fonts
categories:: Notation
related:: Classes/MITHNoteViewer, Classes/MITHUnicode

description:
Part of a project for displaying Common Western Music Notation in SuperCollider using SMuFL ('Standard Music Font Layout') fonts, https://w3c.github.io/smufl/latest/. The class enables searching for a SMuFL glyph by name, and returns its description and Unicode codepoint. If the GUI is created, the glyph will also be displayed.

note:: This class has the dependencies link::Classes/MITHUnicode::  and a SMuFL font, e.g. Bravura (default) https://github.com/steinbergmedia/bravura/, which includes metadata JSON files, see filePath argument below.
::


classmethods:

method:: new
Creates a SMuFLtools instance.

argument:: filePath
Path to the SMuFL JSON data. If Nil, demo data is used if present at ../data/SMuFL-tools-demo-data.json

argument:: verbose
Boolean, posts further information to the Post Window for some class instance methods.

argument:: fontName
A SMuFL font name String

discussion::
code::
f = SMuFLtools.new
::


instancemethods::

private:: setGlyphName
private:: reset
private:: glyphInfo
private:: pathErrorMsg
private:: createDictionary
private:: checkJSON
private:: searchStr

method:: filePath
Returns the path of the loaded JSON data file

method:: verbose
Get or set verbose mode after class has been instantiated

method:: dictGlyphClasses
Returns A Dictionary of all glyphs from the JSON file


subsection:: GUI

method:: pathFinder
Conveniance method, opens a GUI picker to select a JSON data file

method:: gui
Makes a GUI Window to navigate SMuFL glyphs.

argument:: scale
A Float representing the scaling factor for the GUI window. Default is 1.0, allows larger values.

argument:: usePtSize
A Boolean that determines whether font sizes are interpreted as points (true) or pixels (false). Default is false. See discussion in link::Classes/Font::.

discussion::
Creates an instance of link::Classes/SMuFLtoolsGUI::. N.B. It is not necessary to use this class directly other than via this method.
code::
f = SMuFLtools.new;
// a larger window
f.gui(2);
::


subsection:: Selecting a glyph

method:: selectGlyph
Selects a glyph and calls postGlyphInfo
argument:: name
The name of the selected glyph, as either a String or Symbol
discussion:::
code::
f = SMuFLtools.new;
f.selectGlyph(\accidentalSharp)
::

method:: postGlyphInfo
Posts the name and Unicode codepoint of a selected glyph as an Association.
discussion:::
code::
f = SMuFLtools.new;
f.selectGlyph(\gClef);
f.postGlyphInfo // ("gClef" -> "U+E050")
::


method:: glyphName
Returns the name of a selected glyph

method:: glyphCodepoint
Returns a String of the codepoint of a selected glyph

method:: glyphDesc
Returns the SMuFL description of a selected glyph

method:: postGlyphDict
Returns Posts the Dictionary of the selected glyph data


subsection:: Searching

method:: search
search for a glyph

argument:: str
A String to be searched for within the glyph names Dictionary
Returns prints how many matches (if any) are found

method:: printSearchResults
Pretty print search results.
Returns prints a list of matches, with index for selecting glyph

method:: searchKeys
Returns an Array of glyph name matches from a search


method:: glyphIndex
Sets the current glyph
argument:: index
An Integer to select a glyph from a list of returned search results

method:: clear
clears the current search

examples::

code::

// Check if default font Bravura is installed
Font.availableFonts.collect({|i| (i == "Bravura")}).includes(true)

// A small demo subset of SMuFL font metadata in JSON form is provided with the class.
// This can be used to test class functionality

// Otherwise, download of the complete SMuFL font metadata, under 'Releases', is avaialable here:
"https://github.com/w3c/smufl".openOS

// If filePath argument is nil, demo JSON data is loaded
f = SMuFLtools.new

// or, eg.: f = SMuFLtools.new("/path/to/my/JSON/file/glyphnames.json")

// or select a different JSON data file
f.pathFinder // GUI picker

// GUI may be useful, is optional
f.gui(usePtSize: true)

// select a glyph directly by its full name
f.selectGlyph(\noteheadWhole)
f.selectGlyph(\gClef)

// repost glyph info
f.postGlyphInfo

// search for a glyph
f.search("clef")

f.clear // clears search

// partial glyph search terms OK
f.search("note")

f.search("acc")

// show all results in Post Window
// by default all keys if no search performed
f.printSearchResults // pretty print, gives index of result also

f.searchKeys // Array

// navigate to the second search result via code
f.glyphIndex_(1) // to update glyph properties

// selected glyph properties
f.glyphName
f.glyphCodepoint
f.glyphDesc

// Dictionary of data for selected glyph
f.postGlyphDict



















::
